{# /admin/users/<id>: everything about one person, a panel at a time.

   The table behind it says who there is; this says what they are. Every box
   here carries a label the eye can read, because these fields used to sit in
   a row of that table where a placeholder was the only thing telling them
   apart — and a placeholder disappears the moment somebody types.

   Four forms rather than one, for the reason there were four before: an email
   address is private to the site and a profile is the public face, a notice
   switch is a button and how often it arrives is a select, and a password is
   about whoever is signed in. Each saves what its own heading is about and
   lands back here, so a Save always shows its own result. #}
{% extends "layouts/shell.njk" %}
{% import "components/fields.njk" as field %}

{% block title %}Edit {{ account.username }}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  <h1>Edit {{ account.username }}{% if account.you %} <span class="admin-status">(you)</span>{% endif %}</h1>

  <p class="admin-hint"><a href="{{ usersUrl }}">Back to all users</a></p>

  <form class="admin-settings" method="post" action="{{ userEmailUrl }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}" />
    <input type="hidden" name="{{ fields.userId }}" value="{{ account.id }}" />

    <h2>Account</h2>

    <p class="admin-field-static">
      Signs in as <strong>{{ account.username }}</strong>, and writes at
      <a href="{{ account.archiveUrl }}">{{ account.archiveUrl }}</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="admin-hint">
      A username is not editable: it is the login, the author URL above, and
      the actor a follower holds. Somebody who needs a different one is a new
      account.
    </p>
    {# The id they were published under somewhere else (TASK-69). Read-only on
       purpose: it is what the fediverse already holds, and changing it would
       orphan every follow. #}
    {% if account.storedActorId %}
      <p class="admin-hint">
        Also <code>{{ account.storedActorId }}</code> — what the fediverse knows
        this user by. Set by the import or by hand in
        <code>data/users.json</code>, never here.
      </p>
    {% endif %}

    {% set emailHint %}
      {% if mailConfigured %}
        Optional, and never shown on the public site. It is what a forgotten password is recovered through and where the notices below go. Empty it to stop the site writing to this person at all.
      {% else %}
        Optional, and this site sends no mail yet, so nothing will be sent to one. Choose a provider on <a href="{{ adminUrl }}/settings/email">Settings &rsaquo; Email</a> to turn password recovery on.
      {% endif %}
    {% endset %}
    {{ field.text('user-email', fields.email, 'Email address', account.email,
         type='email', autocomplete='email', hint=emailHint) }}

    <p class="admin-settings-buttons">
      <button type="submit">Save email address</button>
    </p>
  </form>

  {# The public face of this person (TASK-67). Anybody's, not only your own:
     there is one role, so an admin who has just added a colleague can put a
     name and a line about them on their archive without waiting for them to
     sign in. After decision-14 these same fields are what their ActivityPub
     actor carries, which is why they live beside the account rather than in
     the site settings — and why saving them tells their followers. #}
  <form class="admin-settings" method="post" action="{{ userProfileUrl }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}" />
    <input type="hidden" name="{{ fields.userId }}" value="{{ account.id }}" />

    <h2>Profile</h2>

    <p class="admin-hint">
      A profile is public. Nothing in it is required — a user with no profile
      still has an archive under their username — and a box left empty is a
      field they do not have.
    </p>

    {% if profileProblems.links %}
      <p class="admin-error">
        Nothing was saved. Fix the Links box below and save again; every other
        box here still holds what you typed.
      </p>
    {% endif %}

    {{ field.text('profile-display-name', fields.displayName, 'Display name',
         account.profile.displayName,
         hint='Printed instead of the login: it heads the archive and is the byline under their posts.') }}

    {{ field.textarea('profile-bio', fields.bio, 'Bio', account.profile.bio, rows='4',
         hint='A line or two about them, shown on the archive under the name.') }}

    {% set avatarHint %}A path such as <code>/uploads/2026/09/me.jpg</code>, or a full URL.{% endset %}
    {{ field.text('profile-avatar', fields.avatar, 'Avatar', account.profile.avatar,
         hint=avatarHint) }}

    {{ field.text('profile-job-title', fields.jobTitle, 'Job title', account.profile.jobTitle,
         hint='What they do, printed beside the name on the archive.') }}

    {{ field.text('profile-location', fields.location, 'Location', account.profile.location,
         hint='Where they are, as they write it.') }}

    {# What the box takes, and the one thing about it nothing on the screen
       used to say (TASK-112): these links are published with rel="me", which
       is what a person deciding what to put here needs to know, and why a
       profile link is not spelled the way a menu item is. #}
    {% set linksHint %}
      One per line, either <code>Label | https://example.com</code> or a bare
      URL that labels itself. A URL is a path like <code>/about/</code> or a
      full <code>http://</code> or <code>https://</code> one, with no spaces in
      it.
      Every link here is published with <code>rel="me"</code>: it is how
      Mastodon verifies a profile field that points back at this site, and how
      IndieAuth knows these are yours. Nothing else in Geekity needs it.
      A menu line on <a href="{{ adminUrl }}/navigation">Navigation</a> ends
      <code>| me</code> to ask for that; a profile link takes no flag, because
      it already carries one.
    {% endset %}
    {{ field.textarea('profile-links', fields.links, 'Links', account.profile.links, rows='4',
         hint=linksHint, error=profileProblems.links) }}

    <p class="admin-settings-buttons">
      <button type="submit">Save profile</button>
    </p>
  </form>

  {# Only once there is both somewhere to write to and something to write
     with. These switches decide what is sent to the address above, so without
     an address, or without a mail provider on Settings > Email, every one of
     them could be on and the site would still send this person nothing. The
     lines below say which is missing where the panel would have been, rather
     than letting it vanish without explanation. #}
  {% if account.email and mailConfigured %}
  <section class="admin-settings">
    <h2>Email {{ account.username }} about</h2>

    <p class="admin-hint">
      What this site writes to {{ account.username }} at <code>{{ account.email }}</code>.
    </p>

    {# One form per switch, not one form with a checkbox each: a browser sends
       no field for an unticked box, so a single form could not tell "turned
       this off" from "left it alone". Adding a notice is one entry in the
       registry and no change here. #}
    {% for notice in account.notifications %}
      <div class="admin-notice">
        <h3>{{ notice.label }}</h3>
        <p class="admin-hint">{{ notice.description }}</p>

        <form class="admin-inline" method="post" action="{{ userNotificationsUrl }}">
          <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}" />
          <input type="hidden" name="{{ fields.userId }}" value="{{ account.id }}" />
          <input type="hidden" name="{{ fields.event }}" value="{{ notice.name }}" />
          <input type="hidden" name="{{ fields.on }}" value="{% if notice.on %}{% else %}1{% endif %}" />
          <span class="admin-status">{% if notice.on %}On{% else %}Off{% endif %}</span>
          <button type="submit">{% if notice.on %}Turn off{% else %}Turn on{% endif %}</button>
        </form>

        {# And, for a notice the registry says can be batched, how often it
           should arrive. A second form because a select needs a Save beside
           it and the switch above is a button; the registry decides which
           notices get one. #}
        {% if notice.batched %}
          <form class="admin-inline" method="post" action="{{ userNotificationModeUrl }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}" />
            <input type="hidden" name="{{ fields.userId }}" value="{{ account.id }}" />
            <input type="hidden" name="{{ fields.event }}" value="{{ notice.name }}" />
            {% call field.select('notice-mode-' + notice.name, fields.mode, 'How often') %}
              {% for choice in notice.modes %}
                <option value="{{ choice.value }}"{% if choice.chosen %} selected{% endif %}>{{ choice.label }}</option>
              {% endfor %}
            {% endcall %}
            <button type="submit">Save</button>
          </form>
          <p class="admin-hint">
            On an hourly or a daily digest nothing is sent as they arrive;
            instead one message a window lists everything still waiting, and
            no message goes at all when nothing is.
          </p>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% else %}
  <section class="admin-settings">
    <h2>Email {{ account.username }} about</h2>

    {% if not mailConfigured %}
      <p class="admin-hint">
        Nothing, while this site has no mail provider: there is nothing to send
        with. Choose one on <a href="{{ adminUrl }}/settings/email">Settings
        &rsaquo; Email</a> and what to send comes back here.
      </p>
    {% else %}
      <p class="admin-hint">
        Nothing, while the box above is empty: there is nowhere to write to.
        Give {% if account.you %}yourself{% else %}this account{% endif %} an
        address and what to send comes back here.
      </p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# Only on your own page: it asks for the current password, so it is about
     whoever is signed in and means nothing on somebody else's screen.
     Resetting a colleague's password from under them is deliberately not
     offered — a fresh account is what that is for. #}
  {% if account.you %}
    <form class="admin-settings" method="post" action="{{ changePasswordUrl }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}" />

      <h2>Change your password</h2>

      {% if passwordProblems.currentPassword or passwordProblems.newPassword %}
        <p class="admin-error">Your password was not changed. Fix the fields marked below and try again.</p>
      {% endif %}

      {{ field.password('current-password', fields.currentPassword, 'Current password',
           error=passwordProblems.currentPassword, autocomplete='current-password',
           required=true) }}

      {{ field.password('new-password', fields.newPassword, 'New password',
           error=passwordProblems.newPassword, autocomplete='new-password', required=true) }}

      {{ field.password('new-password-confirmation', fields.newPasswordConfirmation,
           'New password again', autocomplete='new-password', required=true) }}

      <p class="admin-hint">Every other browser signed in as you is signed out. This one stays.</p>

      <p class="admin-settings-buttons">
        <button type="submit">Change password</button>
      </p>
    </form>
  {% endif %}

  <section class="admin-settings">
    <h2>Delete</h2>

    {# Either the button or the reason there is none, never both: the screen
       does not offer an action it is about to refuse. #}
    {% if deleteRefusal %}
      <p class="admin-hint">{{ deleteRefusal }}</p>
    {% else %}
      <p class="admin-hint">
        Deleting {{ account.username }} signs out every browser they are in and
        cannot be undone. What they have written stays where it is.
      </p>
      <form method="post" action="{{ deleteUserUrl }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}" />
        <input type="hidden" name="{{ fields.userId }}" value="{{ account.id }}" />
        <button type="submit">Delete {{ account.username }}</button>
      </form>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
{% endblock %}
